From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:48:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: pmdomain: Treat unconstrained CPU wake latency
 as unlimited

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

cpu_system_power_down_ok() converts the CPU resume-latency QoS value to
nanoseconds before comparing it with genpd state latency. However,
PM_QOS_RESUME_LATENCY_NO_CONSTRAINT is a sentinel rather than a finite
microsecond limit. Treating it as an ordinary value can reject a valid
state whose combined latency is larger than the converted sentinel.

Detect the sentinel before conversion and allow any state latency when no
constraint is present. Continue enforcing zero and finite latency requests
normally.

Fixes: 8e7de6dc4209 ("pmdomain: Respect the CPU system wakeup QoS limit for s2idle")
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit f0df0192aa22272af6b97ec1c5a891a53e943e4d resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00622
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@fd059f2e0f6257d78e66ce8abb072c398ff066bb
---
 drivers/pmdomain/governor.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c b/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
index 96737abbb496..fc86190ca808 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
@@ -427,8 +427,10 @@ static bool cpu_power_down_ok(struct dev_pm_domain *pd)
 
 static bool cpu_system_power_down_ok(struct dev_pm_domain *pd)
 {
-	s64 constraint_ns = cpu_wakeup_latency_qos_limit() * NSEC_PER_USEC;
 	struct generic_pm_domain *genpd = pd_to_genpd(pd);
+	s32 constraint_us = cpu_wakeup_latency_qos_limit();
+	bool no_constraint;
+	s64 constraint_ns;
 	int state_idx = genpd->state_count - 1;
 
 	if (!(genpd->flags & GENPD_FLAG_CPU_DOMAIN)) {
@@ -436,12 +438,17 @@ static bool cpu_system_power_down_ok(struct dev_pm_domain *pd)
 		return true;
 	}
 
+	no_constraint = constraint_us == PM_QOS_RESUME_LATENCY_NO_CONSTRAINT;
+	constraint_ns = no_constraint ? PM_QOS_RESUME_LATENCY_NO_CONSTRAINT_NS :
+			(s64)constraint_us * NSEC_PER_USEC;
+
 	/* Find the deepest state for the latency constraint. */
 	while (state_idx >= 0) {
 		s64 latency_ns = genpd->states[state_idx].power_off_latency_ns +
 				 genpd->states[state_idx].power_on_latency_ns;
 
-		if (latency_ns <= constraint_ns) {
+		/* The no-constraint value is a sentinel, not a latency budget. */
+		if (no_constraint || latency_ns <= constraint_ns) {
 			genpd->state_idx = state_idx;
 			return true;
 		}
